---
import Figure from "../Figure.astro";
---
<Figure
  width="full"
  stage
  title="Four ways to search the same landscape"
  sub="A toy task, the same budget of 200 evaluations for each. Height is the score; the glowing line marks where solutions are valid; the white dot is the starting program and the glow on the peak is the best known value."
>
  <Fragment slot="controls">
    <span class="seglab">SCiEL uses</span>
    <div class="seg chips" id="mcomp"><button data-c="policy" class="on">Learned policy</button><button data-c="world" class="on">World model</button><button data-c="culture" class="on">Culture</button><button data-c="research" class="on">Research cells</button></div>
    <button class="playb" id="mplay">Play</button>
  </Fragment>
  <div id="mech3d" class="three"><canvas id="cmech"></canvas><div class="ov" id="ovmech"></div></div>
  <div class="racebar"><input class="rng" type="range" id="mT" min="0" max="200" step="1" value="200" aria-label="Evaluation" /><span class="num" id="mTv"></span></div>
  <div class="legend">
    <span><i style="background:#3A6EA5"></i><i style="background:#D0702F;margin-left:-3px"></i><i style="background:#3F8F5C;margin-left:-3px"></i>demes or climbers</span>
    <span><i class="ln" style="background:var(--fig-ink2)"></i>accepted step</span>
    <span>halo: where the policy proposes next</span>
    <span><i style="background:transparent;border:1.5px solid var(--fig-muted)"></i>screened out by the world model</span>
    <span><i class="ln" style="background:var(--fig-chord)"></i>culture, adopted after a trial</span>
    <span><i class="dash"></i>culture, rejected</span>
    <span><i class="ln" style="background:#6E5BB5"></i>research probe</span>
  </div>
  <div class="mcompare" id="mcompare"></div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <b>Only SCiEL chains steps and shares them.</b> <b>One call</b> samples edits of the starting program independently.
    <b>One climber</b> keeps a single line and accepts improvements. <b>Swarm</b> runs five such lines that share nothing.
    <b>SCiEL</b> runs five demes with a learned proposal policy (the halo around each head), a world model that screens
    proposals before they cost an evaluation (hollow rings), culture that moves a lagging deme to the leader after a
    trial (crimson arcs), and research cells that probe far away when a line stalls (violet arcs). The bars average 30
    trials of each; switch components off to see what each is worth. On this landscape research cells add little,
    because the slope always leads somewhere.
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
